Title: Filter stage: hard-fail when Flag 6 (semantic relevance) cannot run
Created: 2026-07-24
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-07-24T16:20Z HDMX-coding-agent created from corpus-v2 rebuild incident

2026-07-27T07:58Z HDMX-coding-agent note closed on t0317-temporal-coverage: reranker backend raises on missing torch (remediation + --skip-llm opt-out in the message), and run_flagging now seeds llm_irrelevant from this run instead of inheriting it from extended_works.csv — the inherited column is what satisfied the presence-only apply gate and kept the skip silent. Sibling-flag audit per action 2: flags 4 and 5 already degrade explicitly via expected_flag_columns(); this ImportError was the only membership-affecting flag that could vanish untraced.
2026-07-27T10:12Z HDMX-coding-agent note independent review of #1127 (APPROVED) found a residual outside this ticket's exit criteria: is_flagged in corpus_filter.py apply/audit computes membership from whatever FLAG_COLUMNS are present, regardless of --skip-llm. So --skip-llm on an input carrying a stale llm_irrelevant column from a prior pass still lets that column drive removal decisions. Opposite failure direction from the 2026-07-24 incident (stale over-removal, not silent under-removal) and arguably intended ('skip' = do not recompute, not do not use), but undocumented. Not fixed here — filed as 0324.
--- body ---
## Context

During the 2026-07-24 corpus-v2 rebuild, the filter stage ran in an env
without torch/sentence-transformers. Flag 6 (semantic relevance) logged
"Flag 6 skipped … no candidates scored" as a WARNING and the stage exited 0,
shipping a refined corpus inflated by 5,840 wrongly-retained works
(38,166 instead of 33,344). The defect was caught only because the number
swung between passes and was chased by hand (PR #1116 diagnosis).

A silently-degraded corpus is worse than a failed build: every downstream
number (paper, letter, deposit) inherits the inflation unnoticed.

## Actions

1. In the filter script, make an unrunnable Flag 6 a hard error (exit
   non-zero), with the remediation in the message (uv sync --group corpus
   --extra cpu|cu130; PYTHONPATH via make).
2. Audit sibling flags for the same skip-and-continue pattern; same
   treatment for any flag whose absence changes corpus membership.

## Test

- Unit: filter invoked with torch unavailable (mock import failure) exits
  non-zero and names Flag 6 in the error.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Filter cannot exit 0 with a membership-affecting flag skipped
- [x] make check green
